      "id": "4nqu36b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background: Why Europeans Came to India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Vasco da Gama discovered the direct sea route to India via the Cape of Good Hope, arriving at Calicut in 1498 where he was welcomed by King Zamorin.",
        "Francisco de Almeida introduced the 'Blue Water Policy' to make the Portuguese the masters of the Indian Ocean.",
        "Alfonso de Albuquerque acquired Goa from the Sultan of Bijapur in 1510, establishing it as the center of Portuguese rule in India.",
        "The Dutch established their first factory at Masulipatnam in 1605, but their power ended after the Battle of Bedara in 1759 against the British.",
        "The English East India Company received its charter from Queen Elizabeth I in 1600 and established its first permanent factory at Surat in 1613.",
        "The French East India Company was formed in 1664 by Colbert, establishing their first factory at Surat in 1668 and key stronghold at Pondicherry."
      ],
      "id": "mjzwbfq"
    },
