      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "First Factories: Portuguese at Cochin (1503), Dutch at Masulipatnam (1605), English at Surat (1613), French at Surat (1668).",
        "Decisive Battles: Battle of Bedara (1759) defeated the Dutch; Battle of Wandiwash (1760) ended French political ambitions in India.",
        "Royal Ambassadors: Captain William Hawkins visited Jahangir's court in 1608, followed by Sir Thomas Roe in 1615 who secured trade concessions for the British.",
        "Carnatic Wars: A series of three military conflicts between the British and French East India Companies from 1746 to 1763."
